        "POSSIBLE COMPLICATIONS": {
          "present": true,
          "status": "content",
          "source_heading": "POSSIBLE COMPLICATIONS",
          "canonical_heading": "POSSIBLE COMPLICATIONS",
          "content_blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Possible complications postoperatively—longterm difficulty prehending food, local recurrence.",
              "pdf_page": 1372,
              "printed_page": 1290,
              "column": 2
            }
          ]
        },
        "EXPECTED COURSE AND PROGNOSIS": {
          "present": true,
          "status": "content",
          "source_heading": "EXPECTED COURSE AND PROGNOSIS.",
          "canonical_heading": "EXPECTED COURSE AND PROGNOSIS",
          "content_blocks": [
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Surgical—generally inoperable in cats; aggressive excision warranted in dogs;",
              "pdf_page": 1372,
              "printed_page": 1290,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Prognosis—poor, owing to extensive local function of the tongue after recuperation is disease (cat) and local recurrence (28% for all usually acceptable in dogs, but will require lingual tumors) and moderate rate of changes in husbandry practices. metastasis (dog).",
              "pdf_page": 1372,
              "printed_page": 1290,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Postsurgical care (e.g., esophagostomy) by",
              "pdf_page": 1372,
              "printed_page": 1290,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "After surgical excision (subtotal glossectomy, owner often required. dogs)—median survival 216 days, <25%",
              "pdf_page": 1372,
              "printed_page": 1290,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Partial glossectomy—may be performed on survive 1 year. the rostral half (mobile tongue) or longitudinal",
              "pdf_page": 1372,
              "printed_page": 1290,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Negative prognostic factors (dogs)—caudal half of the tongue (40–60% removed); location, incomplete excision, recurrence, ~35–50% of patients have incomplete larger size (>2 cm); histologic grade, surgical margins. metastatic disease.",
              "pdf_page": 1372,
              "printed_page": 1290,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Subtotal glossectomy may be considered in",
              "pdf_page": 1372,
              "printed_page": 1290,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Piroxicam—17% response rate in oral SCC select cases. with a median progression-free interval of",
              "pdf_page": 1372,
              "printed_page": 1290,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Other surgical methods (e.g., electrocautery 3.5–6 months; one partial response in 3 dogs and cryosurgery) do not offer additional with lingual SCC. advantage to conventional excision.",
              "pdf_page": 1372,
              "printed_page": 1290,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Prognosis in cats similar to other oral sites",
              "pdf_page": 1372,
              "printed_page": 1290,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Response to radiotherapy—poor (<7 weeks); of SCC; median survival ~3 months with may be used adjunctively on microscopic multimodal therapy. disease postoperatively.",
              "pdf_page": 1372,
              "printed_page": 1290,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Systemic therapies—chemotherapy agents or toceranib phosphate effective in oral SCC may exert anticancer activities for lingual SCC.",
              "pdf_page": 1372,
              "printed_page": 1290,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Piroxicam may have antineoplastic activity",
              "pdf_page": 1372,
              "printed_page": 1290,
              "column": 2
            }
          ]
        }
      }
